About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our Data, AI, Solutions and Engineering practice are looking for Consultants, Senior Consultants and Managers to join the team. &nbsp;

The interface between organisations and their data is being rebuilt. Static dashboards remain useful, but they now sit alongside conversational analytics, dynamically generated insight, analytical applications and agents embedded into operational workflows. Making these experiences valuable requires more than an LLM demo. They need trusted data and semantics, robust analytics engineering, appropriate architecture and a deep understanding of how products will be used. &nbsp;

We are looking for Agentic Analytics Engineers who are strong analytics engineers first and are already applying AI to how they work. You will build analytical products using SQL, Python, semantic and metric models and modern analytics platforms, while also developing Insight Agents, conversational experiences and AI-enabled applications. If you already have substantial delivery experience in agentic analytics, generative BI or LLM-enabled insight, that is highly valuable. We do not, however, expect every strong candidate to have deployed all these capabilities extensively at enterprise scale. &nbsp;

This is a hands-on engineering role. Across all grades we value people who understand how things are built and can show that they are actively experimenting with AI-enabled analytics in practice. In the UK profile, we also put significant weight on consulting and advisory credibility: working directly with clients, making sense of ambiguous problems, shaping architecture and explaining the trade-offs behind technical choices. &nbsp;

What you will be doing

• Understand the business outcome, decision or workflow that the analytical capability needs to improve, and translate that into a robust technical solution. &nbsp;

• Design and build Insight Agents, conversational analytics and AI-enabled analytical applications that connect users to trusted enterprise data and tools. &nbsp;

• Ensure that any AI is explainable and aligns with the relevant guidelines and guardrails that have been define d. &nbsp;

• Design and engineer semantic and metric models so that business definitions, dimensions and measures can be used consistently across BI, applications and AI agents. &nbsp;

